  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1154 PM CDT Tue Aug 4 2026\n\nShower/storm chances... Latest surface obs show the cold front\ndraped over southeast Wisconsin early this morning, resulting in\nweak radar returns percolating mainly in the Fox Valley eastward.\nCAMs show additional shower activity persisting north of the \nslow-moving boundary through this afternoon as transient \nshortwave energy passes over Wisconsin. A rumble or two of thunder\nwill be possible mainly over east-central Wisconsin later this \nmorning, though chances diminish into the afternoon.\n\nNot many changes to speak of regarding late week rain/storm \nchances as we remain on the northeast periphery of western \nridge/heat dome. Most long-range models have the reservoir of \ninstability under the ridge remaining off to our south through the\nweekend, which would shunt better chances for more organized \nconvection to southern Wisconsin and northern Illinois.\nNevertheless, several perturbations embedded within the mean flow\nare progged to interact with a surface low as it tracks over the \nupper Mississippi Valley, kicking off several rounds of shower and\nstorm activity across the forecast area Friday afternoon through \nMonday. ML guidance continues to paint broad 5 to 15% probs over \nthe Midwest on Days 4, 5, and 6. Worth mentioning is the fact that\nstorm predictability remains low this far out, with the synoptic \npattern wont to change over the next couple of days. Will continue\nto monitor for any severe weather potential.\n\nTemperatures/smoke... Temperatures to read near normal in the low\nto mid 80s through the weekend as upper flow flattens out and \nweakens. Humidity levels will be comfortable, with dewpoints \nreading mainly in the low 60s. Some elevated smoke may linger \nacross the area through this evening as the front slowly treks \nsouth, though no significant impacts to visibility or air quality \nare expected.",
